calendar-plus (1.0.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Move remaining generic string and UTF-8 validation mechanics onto
    Infiltratr Common 1.15.5.
  * Collapse duplicate Calendar floor/modulo and named-date helper code.
  * Reuse one set of Gregorian/Julian month-length helpers across providers.
  * Harden wide chronology and calendar-navigation arithmetic against signed
    overflow using Common checked/saturating primitives.
  * Keep chronology, astronomy, historical-calendar rules, ICU probing policy
    and event semantics inside Calendar Plus rather than leaking them into
    Common.
  * Retain the native-installer downgrade handling introduced for the stable
    1.0 version reset.

 -- Shannon Smith <noreply@the-infiltratr.com>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 22:01:00 +1000

calendar-plus (1.0.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Establish Calendar Plus 1.0 as the first stable public release.
  * Ship the completed catalogue of 30 calendar systems and 21 clock choices.
  * Retain the completed MB Corpo typography integration across the panel,
    popup, settings host and native About dialog.
  * Retain the exact Infiltratr Common 1.15.4 public-library dependency.
  * Make the hardware-native .run installer handle the one-time 3.x-to-1.0
    APT version reset automatically instead of failing at install time.
  * Re-anchor the stable v1.0.0 tag and release to the clean single-commit
    1.0 source history and verify that only main and v1.0.0 remain.

